{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>ויגז</b> — two times in the Masorah: ויגז שלוים and the other ויגז ראשו in Job. This is the climax in the midrash: more than Moses — who killed them through the quail by eating, he killed them through descent and falling, that it fell upon their heads, just as is stated in Job ויגז ראשו — and he was mourning over his sons, that the house fell upon them; so here, they were mourning over those who died from the falling of the quail. Ketiv: שלוים; qere: סלוים. שלוים for the righteous, and סלוים for the wicked, for it was to them like thorns."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:56.801373162Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}